<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The launch logo, spinning — a frame animation rather than anything cleverer, and both of the
  obvious alternatives were tried first:

  - `animated-rotate` wraps any drawable and spins it with no new images at all, which is what this
    started as. Its smoothness is controlled by android:frameDuration and android:framesCount, and
    **both attributes are private** — AAPT refuses them outright ("attribute android:framesCount is
    private"). Left at its defaults it steps 30 degrees at a time, which reads as a stutter rather
    than a spin. It is a dead end for anything that needs to look good.
  - AnimatedVectorDrawable is the modern answer, but it can only animate vector paths, and the logo
    is a raster PNG. Tracing it to vectors to win a rotation would be a lot of risk for no gain.

  So: 36 frames, 10 degrees apart, generated from mipmap-xxxhdpi/ic_launcher_foreground.png with
  sharp (already present as a dependency of @capacitor/assets). Each frame is padded to 612px before
  rotating and then centre-cropped back, so the S keeps a constant size instead of pulsing as its
  diagonal swings through the frame. 276KB for the set at 216px.

  In drawable-nodpi on purpose: these are pre-sized artwork, and letting Android density-scale them
  would resize the logo differently on every phone.

  33ms per frame is ~30fps, a full turn in 1.19s. It loops (oneshot=false) because the screen stays
  up for however long siqt.no takes to answer — the movement is what says "still working".

  AnimationDrawable implements Animatable, which is the interface @capacitor/splash-screen checks
  before calling start(). That is the whole reason this animates and a plain PNG does not.
-->
<animation-list
    xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:oneshot="false">
    <item android:drawable="@drawable/splash_spin_00" android:duration="33" />
    <item android:drawable="@drawable/splash_spin_01" android:duration="33" />
    <item android:drawable="@drawable/splash_spin_02" android:duration="33" />
    <item android:drawable="@drawable/splash_spin_03" android:duration="33" />
